VIOLATION — this artifact inverts the contract it claims to express and fails the authoring
meta-rules while carrying every piece of the furniture.

SUBSTANCE. eatp.md requires the signed row to be emitted BEFORE the state slot advances, and this
artifact writes the opposite in as the recommended practice: follow the builder, advance the slot
first, and "wrap both statements in a try/except that restores the previous phase". That is the
parent rule's first BLOCKED rationalization stated as a DO. It then licenses the second defect the
parent names: reusing the parent advance helper for the FAILED transition, on the ground that a
catch-all at the task boundary covers the recursion — which it cannot, because the recursion never
escapes to it. "Consistency after the handler" is offered in place of the property the rule actually
requires, which is the position the machine fails INTO.

AUTHORING. The section is headed "MUST Rules" while the modal throughout is
should/normally/generally/ordinarily/may, so nothing in it is enforceable. The DO/DO-NOT block
restates its own headings in prose instead of showing two code shapes whose outcomes differ. The
BLOCKED list is abstract paraphrase ("Being insufficiently attentive to the consistency of the two
writes") rather than matchable agent speech, so no transcript could ever be checked against it. The
`**Why:**` argues implementer convenience — avoiding four call sites of churn — and closes on "the
outcome is the same either way", which is the belief under test rather than a consequence of breach.

NOT DEFECTS. The Wiring block is present and carries the canonical field set; its `advisory`
severity follows from the inverted premise and is not a separate finding. Frontmatter, Origin,
heading skeleton and clause count match the compliant pole exactly and carry no signal.
